 'A generic write-in line/mark is not a fourth named candidate or proof of a valid named vote. Current§49.99 distinguishes writing a name and, for optical scan, marking its target;§49.98 governs indeterminate choices. County canvass§50.24 separately reports qualifying names and collective scattering under its printed thresholds. Preserve named choices, generic/scattering, under/over, ballots and registration as different categories. '+citation('law-49.99','§49.99')+', '+citation('law-49.98','§49.98')+', '+citation('law-50.24','§50.24')+'.','',
 '**Counting stages and exceptions, source-scoped research.** Current2026 Code§50.45 declares the greatest-vote recipient elected; this is a plurality contest, with tie handling under§50.44. Regular general polls are7am–8pm under§49.73, also stated in the September official November notice and current county notices. Local November3 closing is8pm Central Standard Time (UTC−06:00); the retained local Washington page explicitly uses CST. Date/file/fetch clocks are not votes-as-of clocks. '+citation('law-50.45','§50.45')+', '+citation('law-50.44','§50.44')+', '+citation('law-49.73','§49.73')+', '+citation('county-19183-linked2','Washington official elections page')+'.','',
